# Example `packages` file for set-me-up-omarchy-modules
#
# Rename this file to `packages` (no extension) inside a directory under
# this repo and it will be picked up by install.sh, which finds every
# `packages` file in this tree and installs it via `dotbrains/utilities`'s
# pacman::pacman_install_from_file (aliased as pacman_install_from_file).
#
# This is a comment-only example: nothing is installed by default. Fill in
# your own entries once you know what you actually want on your Omarchy
# machine -- don't rely on a curated list guessed ahead of time.
#
# Format (one directive per line):
#
#   pacman "package-name"                       # install from the official repos
#   aur "package-name"                          # install from the AUR (default helper: yay)
#   aur "package-name" [helper: "yay"]          # install from the AUR with an explicit helper
#   remove "package-name"                       # remove a package (via pacman -Rns)
#
# Lines starting with `#` are comments and are ignored.
#
# Example (uncomment and edit to use):
#
# pacman "ripgrep"
# aur "visual-studio-code-bin"
# aur "spotify" [helper: "yay"]
# remove "some-unwanted-package"
